From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nvr <nvr@localhost>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 05:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] NVR: RESZ depth resolve on every GPU vendor

DXVK offers AMD's RESZ depth-resolve hack (the format check and the
D3DRS_POINTSIZE trigger) only when the adapter reports AMD. The resolve
itself is DXVK's own image copy (D3D9DeviceEx::ResolveZ), so it works on
any GPU. NVR reads the game's depth through RESZ; on NVIDIA it fell back
to NVAPI, which cannot reach a DXVK device, so every depth-based NVR
effect saw an empty depth buffer under DXVK on NVIDIA (found 2026-10-26
with BloodFluid on a GTX 1070; the same picture as d3d9.customVendorId =
1002, which makes DXVK report AMD). Applications that never ask for RESZ
are unaffected.
---
 src/d3d9/d3d9_adapter.cpp | 6 +++---
 src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp  | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/d3d9/d3d9_adapter.cpp b/src/d3d9/d3d9_adapter.cpp
--- a/src/d3d9/d3d9_adapter.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d9/d3d9_adapter.cpp
@@ -162,10 +162,10 @@
     // AMD/Intel's driver hack for RESZ
     // (also advertised in D3D8 by AMD drivers,
     // not advertised at all by modern Intel drivers)
+    // NVR: offered on every vendor (the resolve is DXVK's own copy, see D3D9DeviceEx::ResolveZ), so a D3D9 app that
+    // reads depth through RESZ gets it on NVIDIA as well, where it has no other way under DXVK (NVAPI cannot reach DXVK).
     if (unlikely(rt && CheckFormat == D3D9Format::RESZ && surface))
-      return isAmd
-        ? D3D_OK
-        : D3DERR_NOTAVAILABLE;
+      return D3D_OK;

     // Nvidia/Intel's driver hack for ATOC
     if (unlikely(CheckFormat == D3D9Format::ATOC && surface))
diff --git a/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp b/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp
--- a/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp
@@ -2510,7 +2510,7 @@
             // in D3D8 - once supported by Intel as well,
             // however modern drivers do not expose it)
             constexpr uint32_t RESZ = 0x7fa05000;
-            if (unlikely(Value == RESZ && vendorId == amdVendorId)) {
+            if (unlikely(Value == RESZ)) {   // NVR: every vendor (d3d9_adapter.cpp offers RESZ to all)
               ResolveZ();
               break;
             }
